35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The billing is area-based, not headcount. We paid for empty desks last quarter. Plus, every move costs 6,200 yen.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the printer row is nine decibels louder. Also, the physio says chairs take days to adjust properly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,Four to nine minutes every morning. And two weeks of chaos last year. That’s the real price tag.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the survey confirms daylight was the top complaint. The plan gives four windows, three interior walls. That’s the bias.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... the badge records show early arrivals take the good spots. And the new joiners learned by overhearing.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, that daylight bias is expensive. We pay for empty space, yet the layout still favors a few.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, four to nine minutes is a lot. But the physio note worries me more. If we move desks, my chair takes days to feel right again.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, the chair pain is real, but two weeks of chaos? That’s a month of my life gone. We can’t afford that again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, chaos is temporary. The window seats are permanent. We need to decide who gets the light, not just avoid the mess.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, but if the good spots are taken before I arrive, I’m stuck with the bad ones.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, that confirms the risk. @May, the 6,200 yen per move means we must pick a layout that stays put.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I agree the window seats are valuable. But if I have to re-adjust my chair for days, the quiet spot doesn’t matter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, permanent bias is worse than temporary chaos. I need a layout that respects my time, not just the view.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re right. But avoiding chaos doesn’t fix the unfairness. We need a system that distributes the light, not just hides the mess.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I agree. But if I sit next to the quiet people, I never learn the unwritten rules.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, distributing light is fair, but the 6,200 yen per move makes frequent rotation financially impossible. We need stability.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost. But if I sit by the printer, the noise hurts. I just want a quiet, comfortable spot that stays the same.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Victoria, stability is good, but only if it doesn’t lock me into a noisy, inefficient spot. I need a layout that protects my morning gaps.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, stability is the only option that doesn’t bankrupt us. But if we freeze the layout, we must explicitly assign the window seats. No more guessing.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I agree. But if I’m stuck in a corner, I won’t hear the new joiners. I need to be near the center.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
